     "<div><div dir=\"auto\">Hey all-</div><br></div><div><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div>Hope you&#39;re well!  My name is Greg Obert, and I&#39;m a second year clinical psychology student at Rosalind Franklin University.  My advisor and I are trying to run an analysis on personality data with mclust, but we’re having trouble with one of the graphs.  I’m wondering how to get actual numerical values either on our graph or as a separate piece of R output.  We&#39;re trying to compare centered means in our project with another study, but we&#39;d like to use something a little more precise than the &quot;eyeball method.&quot;  Is Mclust able to put the values on the graph itself?  Or is there a way to somehow get the centered means output separately?  I&#39;ll attach the R file with our syntax and graph if you&#39;d like to see those too.  </div><div><br></div><div>Thanks in advance for the help!</div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br>-- <br><div dir=\"ltr\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">Sincerely,<div><br></div><div>Gregory T. Obert, M.Ed., LPC </div><div>Host of <i>Meditations by Gregory T. Obert</i></div><div><a href=\"http://www.gregorytobert.com/\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.gregorytobert.com/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792496131911000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0a06kp7mBKBcM3eMFsfAZT\">www.GregoryTObert.com</a></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">&quot;Go forth and set the world on fire.&quot; - Ignatius Loyola</span><br></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\"><br></span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Follow Me!</span></div><div><span style=\"font-size:12.8px\">Facebook:  <a href=\"http://facebook.com/GregoryTObertAuthor\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://facebook